From e69069468c3aaa4b023683be428b5af565e77f95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 03:32:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] qtgui: fix "Library not loaded: @rpath/librecoll.N.dylib"
 at runtime

librecoll's install name is @rpath/librecoll.<soversion>.dylib (meson's
default for macOS shared libraries). recollindex and the other
meson-built executables work fine because meson manages their rpath
automatically, but the GUI binary is linked by a separate qmake/make
invocation (custom_target + qmkmk.sh) outside that machinery, so it
carried no -rpath at all: it ran from the build directory (linked
there against librecoll's absolute build path) but failed to load at
its installed location, e.g. /opt/local/bin/recoll on MacPorts.

Add -Wl,-rpath,$$PREFIX/lib via QMAKE_LFLAGS in the Darwin branch,
using the PREFIX qmake variable already threaded through from meson's
prefix option.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ddfj6DPA9L8P9ba1f3ULvn
---
 src/qtgui/recoll.pro.in | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/qtgui/recoll.pro.in b/src/qtgui/recoll.pro.in
index 35391ec5..32761433 100644
--- a/src/qtgui/recoll.pro.in
+++ b/src/qtgui/recoll.pro.in
@@ -511,4 +511,12 @@ greaterThan(QT_MAJOR_VERSION, 4) {
   contains( UNAME, SunOS ) {
           LIBS += -ldl
   }
+  contains( UNAME, Darwin ) {
+    # librecoll's install name is "@rpath/librecoll.<soversion>.dylib" (meson's default for
+    # macOS shared libraries). Unlike recollindex and the other meson-built executables, this
+    # binary is linked by qmake/make outside meson's own rpath handling, so without this it
+    # loads fine from the build directory (where qmkmk.sh links it against librecoll's absolute
+    # build path) but fails at its installed location with "Library not loaded: @rpath/....dylib".
+    QMAKE_LFLAGS += -Wl,-rpath,$$PREFIX/lib
+  }
 }
